        in the affected area.", "sourcePage": 2, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1981}, {"number": 9, "prompt": "You should cool burn injuries by taking off any                                       or jewellery that\nthe patient is wearing.\nSAMPLE\n[CANDIDATE NO.] READING QUESTION PAPER PART A 02/04", "sourcePage": 2, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 2197}, {"number": 10, "prompt": "When cooling the wound, make sure that you don’t put the patient at risk\nof                                       .", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 0}, {"number": 14, "prompt": "In the case of mixed depth burns, what factor determines the local treatment to give?\nA", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1073}, {"number": 15, "prompt": "What is the maximum number of tries recommended for attaching a drip at the scene of a burns\nS\nincident?", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1219}, {"number": 16, "prompt": "How much resuscitation fluid should a child receive per kilo over 20kg?", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1406}, {"number": 17, "prompt": "Before attaching a fluid resuscitation drip to a 9-year-old burns patient, what percentage of the body\nneeds to be affected?", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1504}, {"number": 18, "prompt": "What additional analgesic is recommended in the first instance for a patient with a moderate level of\npain?", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1678}, {"number": 19, "prompt": "What route should be used to administer ibuprofen to children?", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1835}, {"number": 20, "prompt": "After how long should a patient’s pain relief regime be re-evaluated?", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1924}], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": ["1f4bf40fdb622fc060ed6726164f9350428422edcfd16b15828a2a00af66d45a"], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-77288c0ac253b20d8fe8", "filename": "Listening-Sample-Test-3-Answer-Key.pdf", "sha256": "77288c0ac253b20d8fe894ba1f330aa93ce9d55ca54b5e774a344b9283f7c75a", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/77288c0ac253b20d8fe894ba1f330aa93ce9d55ca54b5e774a344b9283f7c75a.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/77288c0ac253b20d8fe894ba1f330aa93ce9d55ca54b5e774a344b9283f7c75a.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, {"id": "offline-9c87474cf8022a76f7cb", "filename": "04. Reading-Sample-Test-3-Answer-Key-Part-A.pdf", "sha256": "9c87474cf8022a76f7cb199490e769a131394e8ac52333a7754b23f737ea7435", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/9c87474cf8022a76f7cb199490e769a131394e8ac52333a7754b23f737ea7435.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/9c87474cf8022a76f7cb199490e769a131394e8ac52333a7754b23f737ea7435.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, {"id": "offline-e1a2ca3008877bc11003", "filename": "05. Reading-Sample-Test-3-Answer-Key-Part-BC.pdf", "sha256": "e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}], "passages": [{"sourceSha256": "bfe70c7d6bc2a95e2179549e26c98fad88dac36c36b9bb31111f16566bb88601", "pages": [1, 2, 3, 4]}]}, {"id": "00858a83d20c743d-p1", "label": "03. Reading-Sample-Test-3-Question-Paper-Part-BC.pdf", "part": null, "sourceSha256": "00858a83d20c743d56c697a98807846d9d0c6c7a78b0370b31d347ea673f3708", "pages": [1], "questions": [], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": ["1f4bf40fdb622fc060ed6726164f9350428422edcfd16b15828a2a00af66d45a"], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-77288c0ac253b20d8fe8", "filename": "Listening-Sample-Test-3-Answer-Key.pdf", "sha256": "77288c0ac253b20d8fe894ba1f330aa93ce9d55ca54b5e774a344b9283f7c75a", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/77288c0ac253b20d8fe894ba1f330aa93ce9d55ca54b5e774a344b9283f7c75a.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/77288c0ac253b20d8fe894ba1f330aa93ce9d55ca54b5e774a344b9283f7c75a.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, {"id": "offline-9c87474cf8022a76f7cb", "filename": "04. Reading-Sample-Test-3-Answer-Key-Part-A.pdf", "sha256": "9c87474cf8022a76f7cb199490e769a131394e8ac52333a7754b23f737ea7435", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/9c87474cf8022a76f7cb199490e769a131394e8ac52333a7754b23f737ea7435.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/9c87474cf8022a76f7cb199490e769a131394e8ac52333a7754b23f737ea7435.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, {"id": "offline-e1a2ca3008877bc11003", "filename": "05. Reading-Sample-Test-3-Answer-Key-Part-BC.pdf", "sha256": "e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}], "passages": []}, {"id": "00858a83d20c743d-p2", "label": "Part B · 03. Reading-Sample-Test-3-Question-Paper-Part-BC.pdf", "part": "B", "sourceSha256": "00858a83d20c743d56c697a98807846d9d0c6c7a78b0370b31d347ea673f3708", "pages": [2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7], "questions": [{"number": 2, "prompt": "According to the guidance notes, all staff involved in transferring patients from critical to general care must\nA    obtain all necessary consent from any interested parties.\nB    ensure that the patient’s personal care plan is also transferred.\nC    make arrangements for ongoing co-operation once the transfer is complete.\nE\nTransfer of patients\n1.15\nL\nThe critical care area transferring team and the receiving ward team should take shared responsibility for\nthe care of the patient being transferred. They should jointly ensure that:\nP\n• there is continuity of care through a formal structured handover from critical care area staff to ward\n. staff (including both medical and nursing staff), supported by a written plan;\nM\n• the receiving ward, with support from critical care if required, can deliver the agreed plan.\n1.16\nA\nWhen patients are transferred to the general ward from a critical care area, they should be offered\ninformation about their condition and encouraged to actively participate in decisions that relate to their\nS\nrecovery. The information should be tailored to individual circumstances. If they agree, their family and\ncarers should be involved.\nSAMPLE\n[CANDIDATE NO.] READING QUESTION PAPER PARTS B & C 03/16", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 0, "answer": {"text": "B       ensure that the patient’s personal care plan is also transferred.", "source": {"id": "offline-e1a2ca3008877bc11003", "filename": "05. Reading-Sample-Test-3-Answer-Key-Part-BC.pdf", "sha256": "e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 6, "prompt": "When dealing with patients following a safety incident, staff must avoid\nA    saying anything until the facts have been established.\nB    speculating on the possible causes of the incident.\nC    contradicting what has been said by other staff.\nPatient Safety Incidents\nE\nInformation about a patient safety incident must be given to patients and/or their carers in a truthful\nL\nand open manner by an appropriately nominated person. Patients want a step-by-step explanation of\nwhat happened that considers their individual needs and is delivered openly. Communication must also\nP\nbe timely – patients and/or carers should be provided with information about what happened as soon\nas practicable. It is also essential that any information given is based solely on the facts known at the\nM\ntime. Healthcare staff should explain that new information may emerge as an incident investigation is\nundertaken, and patients and/or their carers will be kept up-to-date with the progress of an investigation.\nA\nThe Duty of Candour Regulations require that information be given as soon as is reasonably practicable\nand be given in writing no later than 10 days after the incident was reported through the local systems.\nS\nSAMPLE\n[CANDIDATE NO.] READING QUESTION PAPER PARTS B & C 07/16", "sourcePage": 7, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 0, "answer": {"text": "B       speculating on the possible causes of the incident.", "source": {"id": "offline-e1a2ca3008877bc11003", "filename": "05. Reading-Sample-Test-3-Answer-Key-Part-BC.pdf", "sha256": "e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": ["1f4bf40fdb622fc060ed6726164f9350428422edcfd16b15828a2a00af66d45a"], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-77288c0ac253b20d8fe8", "filename": "Listening-Sample-Test-3-Answer-Key.pdf", "sha256": "77288c0ac253b20d8fe894ba1f330aa93ce9d55ca54b5e774a344b9283f7c75a", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/77288c0ac253b20d8fe894ba1f330aa93ce9d55ca54b5e774a344b9283f7c75a.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/77288c0ac253b20d8fe894ba1f330aa93ce9d55ca54b5e774a344b9283f7c75a.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, {"id": "offline-e1a2ca3008877bc11003", "filename": "05. Reading-Sample-Test-3-Answer-Key-Part-BC.pdf", "sha256": "e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}], "passages": []}, {"id": "00858a83d20c743d-p8", "label": "Part C · 03. Reading-Sample-Test-3-Question-Paper-Part-BC.pdf", "part": "C", "sourceSha256": "00858a83d20c743d56c697a98807846d9d0c6c7a78b0370b31d347ea673f3708", "pages": [8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 16], "questions": [{"number": 8, "prompt": "In the second paragraph, what point is made about food intolerances?\nL\nA    Scientists continue to disagree about their root causes.\nP\nB    The symptoms are indistinguishable from those of allergies.\nC    They can have an unpredictable impact on the person affected.\nM\nD    The distinction between them and allergies is not widely appreciated.\nA", "sourcePage": 10, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 442, "answer": {"text": "D      The distinction between them and allergies is not widely appreciated.", "source": {"id": "offline-e1a2ca3008877bc11003", "filename": "05. Reading-Sample-Test-3-Answer-Key-Part-BC.pdf", "sha256": "e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 11, "prompt": "In the fifth paragraph, what point is made about the two hypotheses mentioned?\nA    They both appear to be credible.\nB    They directly contradict each other.\nC    They fail to define their terms adequately.\nD    They should both be studied in more depth.\nE", "sourcePage": 11, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 0, "answer": {"text": "They directly contradict each other.", "source": {"id": "offline-e1a2ca3008877bc11003", "filename": "05. Reading-Sample-Test-3-Answer-Key-Part-BC.pdf", "sha256": "e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 12, "prompt": "What does the phrase ‘this rule’ in the fifth paragraph refer to?\nL\nA    the likelihood of having an inherited allergy to certain foods\nP\nB    the type of diet in which food allergies more commonly occur\nC    the degree of contact with allergens needed to trigger a reaction\nM\nD    the order of events most commonly found prior to allergic attacks\nA", "sourcePage": 11, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 426, "answer": {"text": "D      the order of events most commonly found prior to allergic attacks", "source": {"id": "offline-e1a2ca3008877bc11003", "filename": "05. Reading-Sample-Test-3-Answer-Key-Part-BC.pdf", "sha256": "e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 13, "prompt": "What does the sixth paragraph suggest about the transference of allergies between mother and child?\nS\nA    It is only possible with particular individuals.\nB    It can result in instances of malnourishment.\nC    It may be avoidable if certain precautions are taken.\nD    It is most likely to take place before the baby is born.", "sourcePage": 11, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 1092, "answer": {"text": "C      It may be avoidable if certain precautions are taken.", "source": {"id": "offline-e1a2ca3008877bc11003", "filename": "05. Reading-Sample-Test-3-Answer-Key-Part-BC.pdf", "sha256": "e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 15, "prompt": "What information can be found in the first paragraph?\nA    reference to some recent findings relating to heart disease\nB    indication of the greatest risk factor associated with heart disease\nC    mention of a misconception about the chief causes of heart disease\nD    figures showing the country with the highest mortality rate from heart disease\nE", "sourcePage": 14, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 26, "answer": {"text": "A       reference to some recent findings relating to heart disease", "source": {"id": "offline-e1a2ca3008877bc11003", "filename": "05. Reading-Sample-Test-3-Answer-Key-Part-BC.pdf", "sha256": "e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 16, "prompt": "When the writer uses the word ‘cost’ in the second paragraph she is referring to\nL\nA    overwhelming evidence.\nP\nB    placental insufficiency.\nC    viable pregnancy.\nM\nD    reduced growth.\nA", "sourcePage": 14, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 549, "answer": {"text": "D       reduced growth.", "source": {"id": "offline-e1a2ca3008877bc11003", "filename": "05. Reading-Sample-Test-3-Answer-Key-Part-BC.pdf", "sha256": "e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 17, "prompt": "In the third paragraph, what does the author suggest about the work of the international research\nS\ncommunity on this subject?\nA    Their focus has been too narrow.\nB    Some of their studies may be flawed.\nC    There is nothing original about their research.\nD    They were overly keen to seize on a particular idea.", "sourcePage": 14, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 1052, "answer": {"text": "A       Their focus has been too narrow.", "source": {"id": "offline-e1a2ca3008877bc11003", "filename": "05. Reading-Sample-Test-3-Answer-Key-Part-BC.pdf", "sha256": "e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 18, "prompt": "What was the aim of the study described in the fourth paragraph?\nA    to compare neonatal records between the UK and Bolivia\nB    to assess the relative significance of two risk factors for newborns\nC    to find a link between birth weight and predisposition to heart disease\nD    to determine the likelihood of high-altitude babies being carried to full term\nSAMPLE\n[CANDIDATE NO.] READING QUESTION PAPER PARTS B & C 14/16", "sourcePage": 14, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 1506, "answer": {"text": "B       to assess the relative significance of two risk factors for newborns", "source": {"id": "offline-e1a2ca3008877bc11003", "filename": "05. Reading-Sample-Test-3-Answer-Key-Part-BC.pdf", "sha256": "e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 19, "prompt": "What assumption was proved wrong by the results of the study?\nA    Lower-income mothers generally give birth to lower weight babies.\nB    A baby born at high altitude will typically weigh less than one born at sea level.\nC    Levels of oxygen have a greater impact on birth weight than nutritional status does.\nD    There is a correlation between prenatal oxygen levels and predisposition to heart disease.\nE", "sourcePage": 15, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 0, "answer": {"text": "A       Lower-income mothers generally give birth to lower weight babies.", "source": {"id": "offline-e1a2ca3008877bc11003", "filename": "05. Reading-Sample-Test-3-Answer-Key-Part-BC.pdf", "sha256": "e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 20, "prompt": "In the sixth paragraph, what is suggested about the inhabitants of La Paz?\nL\nA    The altitude affects all socio-economic groups in a similar way.\nP\nB    There is a high degree of ethnic diversity at all levels of society.\nC    Most residents have a shared ancestry going back two thousand years.\nM\nD    Poorer residents have a genetic advantage over those with higher incomes.\nA", "sourcePage": 15, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 574, "answer": {"text": "D       Poorer residents have a genetic advantage over those with higher incomes.", "source": {"id": "offline-e1a2ca3008877bc11003", "filename": "05. Reading-Sample-Test-3-Answer-Key-Part-BC.pdf", "sha256": "e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 22, "prompt": "What advantage of the research involving hen eggs is mentioned in the final paragraph?\nA    the availability of supplies\nB    the simplicity of the procedure\nC    the reliability of the data obtained\nD    the speed with which results are seen", "sourcePage": 15, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 1600, "answer": {"text": "D       the speed with which results are seen", "source": {"id": "offline-e1a2ca3008877bc11003", "filename": "05. Reading-Sample-Test-3-Answer-Key-Part-BC.pdf", "sha256": "e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": ["1f4bf40fdb622fc060ed6726164f9350428422edcfd16b15828a2a00af66d45a"], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-77288c0ac253b20d8fe8", "filename": "Listening-Sample-Test-3-Answer-Key.pdf", "sha256": "77288c0ac253b20d8fe894ba1f330aa93ce9d55ca54b5e774a344b9283f7c75a", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/77288c0ac253b20d8fe894ba1f330aa93ce9d55ca54b5e774a344b9283f7c75a.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/77288c0ac253b20d8fe894ba1f330aa93ce9d55ca54b5e774a344b9283f7c75a.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, {"id": "offline-e1a2ca3008877bc11003", "filename": "05. Reading-Sample-Test-3-Answer-Key-Part-BC.pdf", "sha256": "e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/e1a2ca3008877bc11003ea29973cdac4abdbf1569d4750295401feb24974c7cf.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}], "passages": []}, {"id": "80bcfb199d110acf-p1", "label": "Listening-Sample-Test-3-Audio-Script.pdf", "part": null, "sourceSha256": "80bcfb199d110acf6f7bbef230d143db23daf0fc805f9311bea8ef78a9d591ec", "pages": [1], "questions": [], "skills": ["listening"], "recordings": ["1f4bf40fdb622fc060ed67